 By the Remainder Theorem, the remainder when a polynomial is divided by a linear divisor of the form $x - c$ is equal to the value of the polynomial at $x = c.$

Therefore, let $p(x) = x^3 - 3x + 5.$  By the Remainder Theorem, $p(-2) = (-2)^3 - 3(-2) + 5 = \boxed{3}$ is the remainder.

